      "location": "5.1",
      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "Step 5.1 says, “each tooth block B_i has size |B|/ell^2.” But [L3] only yields an (ell,|B|/ell^2)-comb. The cited definition `def-comb-in-a-graph` requires its blocks to form an (ell,w)-blockade, and `def-blockade-length-and-width` defines that as |B_i| >= w, not equality. Thus the asserted exact sizes do not follow and can be false; the available lower bound would suffice for the subsequent inequality.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "accc9e0d41790100e167d04f8d70e5c30b58d35d38d7dd979e271628ee36863b"
    },
