      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "Step 1.1 moves from “there exists at least one real number lambda” to “Choose such a lambda minimal.” The hypotheses establish that lambda=c is admissible, but do not state a minimum principle or derive one. A nonempty subset of the reals need not have a minimum; here finiteness of G can supply a short finite-candidate argument, but that argument is neither given nor cited.",
